  "raw_text": "Step 1: Since \\( p(x) \\) is a monic polynomial of degree 4 and three of its roots are 1, 2, and 3, we can express \\( p(x) \\) in the form:\n\\[ p(x) = (x-1)(x-2)(x-3)(x-r) \\]\nwhere \\( r \\) is the fourth root of the polynomial.\n\nStep 2: To find \\( p(0) \\), substitute \\( x = 0 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[ p(0) = (0-1)(0-2)(0-3)(0-r) = (-1)(-2)(-3)(-r) = 6r \\]\n\nStep 3: To find \\( p(4) \\), substitute \\( x = 4 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[ p(4) = (4-1)(4-2)(4-3)(4-r) = (3)(2)(1)(4-r) = 6(4-r) = 24 - 6r \\]\n\nStep 4: Add \\( p(0) \\) and \\( p(4) \\):\n\\[ p(0) + p(4) = 6r + (24 - 6r) = 24 \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{24}<|im_end|>",
